WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.939 --> 00:00:06.050
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and this week for
my Korra bonus video I wanted to do a breakdown

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:10.179
of all the specialized sub bending techniques.
Book 3 is all about explaining the sub style

00:00:10.179 --> 00:00:14.530
of Airbending via Jinora, so I'll explain
that too. They haven't been super explicit

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.730
when they mentioned it on the show, but Jinora
had a few lines that summed it up.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.230
Hello any new peoples, if you're just finding
me for the first time I do Korra videos every

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.540
week. Be sure to subscribe to get everything.
I'm even doing a special Comic Con giveaway

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.550
that i'll explain at the end of this video.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.950
So up to Book 3 we've seen a substyle for
all the major bending forms. I remember when

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:34.879
Book 2 was getting ready to be released last
year they talked about creating the new substyle

00:00:34.879 --> 00:00:40.629
to Air. But when Book 2 came and went with
no explanation everyone was a little WTF confused.

00:00:40.629 --> 00:00:44.909
Especially when Jinora deus ex machina saved
Raava and Korra in the finale.

00:00:44.909 --> 00:00:49.050
Technically that was the substyle, the way
they showed it in Book 3 looked a little different,

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:53.079
but it's projecting your spirit. Jinora's
words when she was explaining it to Kai were

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:57.170
"It's a high level airbender move, with some
spiritual stuff thrown in."

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:01.260
That actually made me laugh a little because
during the Korra Book 2 dvd commentaries.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:07.630
Mike and Bryan talked about Jinora's Raava
rescue. They explained that they didn't know

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:11.930
what she was doing. They just wanted to see
her resuscitate the little piece of Raava

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:13.630
that was inside UnaVaatu.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:18.980
But for all intents and purposes, think of
the Air substyle as Spirit Bending. Not to

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:24.660
be confused with Energy Bending, which could
be considered a sub-style of all forms of

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:28.490
bending even though it's classified as a separate
form.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:33.290
Jinora having the deepest connection to the
spirit world aside from Korra would of course

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:37.460
be the one to Demo a new style. I love how
the series just brushed over the fact that

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:41.320
she discovered it without any help. Since
we don't see a lot of Jinora scenes I'm guessing

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:46.000
she did sit down and work it out at some point,
Mike and Bryan just decided not to show us

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.030
the montage of her figuring it out.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:55.030
The other interesting thing to note is that
it is a passive ability. It's not used as

00:01:55.380 --> 00:02:00.950
an attack ability like the other sub forms.
Here's a breakdown of all the rest.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:04.810
Next on the cool list right is Combustion.
There's actually three sub forms of fire bending

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:09.280
including lightning generation and lightning
redirection but Sparky Sparky Boom Girl is

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.550
killing it right now, so let's start with
that.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:16.890
Combustion is really the channeling of your
chi through a focused point. Denoted by the

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:21.370
Third Eye Tattoo all Combustion benders have
like Sparky Sparky Boom Man in last airbender

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:28.370
and now P'Li on Korra.
It's more of a focused heat blast than a searing

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:35.120
burn you'd get from regular firebending. It's
true that Azula and other prodigy firebenders

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.840
can bend blue flame which is way hotter. But
in terms of blast damage, Combustion is much

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:40.540
more effective.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:45.959
It's not like a machine gun though, because
you have to focus your chi it takes time to

00:02:45.959 --> 00:02:50.600
generate the attack. If you lose focus, like
when someone throws a boomerang at your face,

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:54.330
the blowback can kill you. Like the kickback
from a giant gun squishing your brains.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:59.680
As of right now on the show, Combustion Man
and the new Red Lotus firebender are the only

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.069
ones known to possess the ability. But it's
not a genetic thing, it's all about spiritual

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:05.480
alignment.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:10.150
Lightning Generation and Redirection are much
more common sub styles. Creating lightning

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:14.240
requires you to separate the positive and
negative energies in your body, like yin and

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.130
yang in a physical sense.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:19.760
When you're able to control the interaction
of postive and negative energy, the bender

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:24.060
guides it outward towards the finger tips
and the resulting charge leaves their body

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:28.340
in the form of electricity. They call it lightning
because it's discharged.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:32.120
The charge of the blasts can be regulated,
like using a dimmer switch on a light bulb.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:39.120
Iroh claims he created Lightning redirection
as an answer to waterbending. Redirecting

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:44.500
the charge using your body as a conduit.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.660
One of the coolest things I saw when I first
started watching Korra was learning that Firebenders

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:54.830
were using Lightning bending to generate electricity
at power stations in Republic City. It totally

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:59.470
makes sense that as bending becomes more sophisticated
it starts being used as a commodity.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:05.910
Bloodbending and Healing are the to Water
Substyles

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:09.930
During Last Airbender Hama claims she's the
first one to figure out Bloodbending. Just

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:14.000
realizing that people are mostly made of water,
but I always wonder if she and Iroh for instance

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.030
are just the first people to be recorded talking
about special bending techniques. So when

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.090
someone says I'm the first ever in the history
of the world, just take it with a grain of

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:24.610
The reason why Yakkone, Amon and Tarrlok were
able to do it without the use of the full

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:29.590
moon was because one, they were just powerful
benders to begin with and two, they had extensive

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:30.080
training.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.810
When bloodbending it looks like you're making
a person move against their will, but really

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:38.500
what your doing is manipulating the liquid
in their bodies. Every organic process in

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:43.750
your body requires water molecules. H20. They
coat membranes that float around in all parts

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:48.330
of your body, most notably around your bones
and your muscles. So by moving those, it makes

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.470
it look like your making their muscles move.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:54.370
The reason it's so hard to do is because you're
focusing on those small molecules that coat

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:55.340
the muscles.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:05:00.410
On the flipside Healing is a slightly less
powerful but way more practical sub form.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:06.160
It involves using the life giving properties
of water in an energy based context. So you

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:10.160
can treat certain types of wounds and because
it's energy based you can detect problems

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.470
with a person's chi.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:16.780
Unalaq was also able to use this to quote
unquote Heal Dark Spirits. I know they didn't

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:20.760
explain that in book 2 very much. But he's
using a slight variation on Katara's healing

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:23.979
ability to calm spirits which he then taught
to Korra.

00:05:23.979 --> 00:05:28.130
Part of the reason I think Korra wasn't able
to heal the spirit vines in Republic City

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:32.280
is because there wasn't anything wrong with
them. If they had been Dark Spirit vines I

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:36.660
think it would have worked. But they weren't
attacking the buildings or going crazy in

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:37.979
an unnatural way.

00:05:37.979 --> 00:05:43.790
Metalbending is also one of my favorite substyles.
In addition Toph and Lin Beifong's Seismic

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.610
ability and Lava Bending are described as
Earth sub styles.

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:52.870
Metalbending is a little bit like Bloodbending
the earth. What you're doing is bending the

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:58.810
trace unprocessed parts of earth elements
in processed metals. So the more impure or

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:02.229
unprocessed a metal is, the easier it is to
bend.

00:06:02.229 --> 00:06:07.729
You're bending the little bits that are unprocessed,
like a Bloodbender bends the little bits of

00:06:07.729 --> 00:06:09.380
water covering your muscles.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:13.460
The reason Toph says she can't bend platinum
is because it's a pure metal, there are no

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:18.320
bits of regular earth left, it would be like
a bloodbender trying to bend sand in the desert.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:21.729
Even though technically at night there is
moisture in the desert air.

00:06:21.729 --> 00:06:26.690
The Seismic ability is something Toph learned
from the badgermoles as a way to navigate.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:32.130
Since she was blind she had to learn to get
around on her own. It does require you to

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:38.080
feel vibrations on naked skin, so that's why
she always walks around without shoes.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.820
I wonder how many times she had to wash her
feet everyday.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:47.880
Lava Bending is something we've seen Gazan
do, this is a small contradiction of the way

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:52.310
it's explained in Last Airbender. During that
series it was explained that only a fully

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:56.669
realized avatar could lava bend because it
involved the concurrent use of firebending

00:06:56.669 --> 00:06:58.039
and earth bending.

00:06:58.039 --> 00:07:01.580
But since we saw Gazan do it on Korra I'm
guessing that a normal bender can heat the

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:06.880
rock just using friction from the air. Gazan
just gets it spinning so fast that the air

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:12.940
friction heats it to melting point and he
fashions it into a superheated blade.

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:17.789
This is pretty small scale though, Avatar
Roku was able to erupt a volcano and Avatar

00:07:17.789 --> 00:07:23.199
Kyoshi used it to separate Kyoshi Island from
the mainland.

00:07:23.199 --> 00:07:28.300
Energy Bending predates all other forms and
currently there's no sub style associated

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.820
with it. That doesn't mean someone won't develop
one eventually. It's when someone bends the

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:35.410
life energy inside a person.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:39.220
Right now we know Energy Bending can be used
to take away or restore a person's bending

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:46.220
and impart knowledge instantly. It's been
suggested that when the Lion Turtles were

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:51.870
giving Bending to people in Avatar Wan's time,
they were doing so using energy bending.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:56.930
So I guess if Korra ever developed the ability,
she could bestow bending on a non-bender.

00:07:56.930 --> 00:08:02.770
But it's still the biggest question mark of
all the bending styles.

